  "query_preview": "..(This Evening Through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1224 PM MDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\n18z surface analysis had weak trough from ND into central WY. \nWater vapour loop had upper ridge over CO/NM and building heights \nover the northern Plains - a distinct wave hard to find. 0.5km \nvisible satellite loop had cu/tcu over Campbell County, and then \nnear the western foothills of the Black Hills per downstream \nconvergence given east/southeast flow on the western SD plains. \nUpper ridge continues to dominate the weather this week.\n\nThis afternoon/evening, 0.5-1KJ/kg MLCAPE will develop over \nnortheastern WY/southwestern SD with 25-35kts effective shear and \nlimited MLCIN. Isolated/scattered tsra will develop with a few \nstorms capable of gusty winds. CAMs not particularly excited about\norganized convective prospect, probably owing to the rising mid- \nlevel heights. Guidance temperatures look fine.\n\nWednesday looks a little more interesting. Distinct shortwave \ntrough will rotate around ridge and reach eastern MT/WY during \npeak insolation, impinging on surface trough. 1-1.5KJ/kg MLCAPE \nwill have 25-35kts 0-6km bulk shear available. Forecast soundings \nsuggest damaging wind will be the main threat, especially over \nnorthwestern SD, but some large hail not out of the question. NBM \nPoPs robust, but seem warranted given available synoptic scale \nforcing. Temperatures will be near guidance.\n\nThursday through the weekend will be very warm/hot. Sunday looks \nhottest right now per robust thermal ridge and preponderance of \nensemble guidance. Perhaps some record highs in jeopardy by \nSunday. Any day could feature active thunderstorms. The \"cooldown\"\nfor the beginning/middle of next week still looks like it is \nthere, but the signal keeps getting muted by differing ensemble \nsolutions. Confidence remains low in sustained heat relief.",
